 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "`src/tessel/debughelpers.py` defines three exceptions:\n\n- **`DebugFilesKeyError`** (L23, subclasses `KeyError` and `AssertionError`)\n  - It is raised by `request.files[key]` when the key is missing from `files` but present in `request.form`.\n  - That usually means the form was posted without `enctype=\"multipart/form-data\"`, and the message says so.\n  - It only happens in debug mode. `Request._load_form_data` (`src/tessel/wrappers.py:202-210`) patches `request.files` via `attach_enctype_error_multidict` when `active_app.debug` is on, the mimetype isn't `multipart/form-data` and `files` is empty.\n\n- **`FormDataRoutingRedirect`** (L50, subclasses `AssertionError`)\n  - It is raised from `Tessel.raise_routing_exception` (`src/tessel/app.py:584-586`).\n  - That happens in debug mode when routing wants to redirect (typically a trailing-slash redirect) and the method isn't GET, HEAD or OPTIONS, and the status isn't 307 or 308.\n  - Such a redirect would make the browser drop the form data.\n\n- **`UnexpectedUnicodeError`** (L17, subclasses `AssertionError` and `UnicodeError`)\n  - It is defined for better reporting of unexpected unicode or binary data.\n  - Nothing in `src/` raises it, so it appears to be unused legacy.",
